The Sol Forge @PROJECT_VERSION@
===============================

The authoring tool for The Stars Don't Wait. It opens a mod folder and lets you
build meshes, paint-in textures, sounds, materials and the def rows that tie
them together, then cooks the lot into the form the game loads.

This is a separate download from the game on purpose. You need both: the game
to play, this to author. Unpack it anywhere; delete the folder to uninstall.


Requirements
------------

@SOL_FORGE_REQUIREMENTS@


Pointing it at a mod
--------------------

The Forge always works on one PROJECT, which is a mod folder inside your game
install:

    <your game folder>/mods/my-mod/

@SOL_FORGE_OPEN@

The first time it opens a folder it creates the layout for you:

    my-mod/
      assets/           what you author       (.forge .tex .png .wav)
        meshes/
        textures/
        sounds/
      cooked/           what the game loads   (.smesh .stex .saud)
      shaders/          compiled SPIR-V       (.spv)
      blender-inbox/    where Send to Forge drops a .glb

Your def rows - models.toml, materials.toml, ships.toml, stations.toml,
sounds.toml - sit at the top of the mod folder, beside assets/. Write only the
ones you need; a mod that changes nothing else does not need the rest.

Press Cook when you have changed an asset. It writes into the mod's cooked/,
which is exactly where the game looks, so there is no copying step. Then start
the game: mods load automatically, in folder-name order.


Shaders need one extra thing
----------------------------

Meshes, textures, sounds and def rows need nothing but this tool. A SHADER is
the exception: a mod ships compiled SPIR-V, and no GLSL compiler is distributed
with the game or with the Forge. To write one you need the Vulkan SDK, and you
compile it yourself:

    glslc --target-env=vulkan1.3 shaders/glass.frag -o shaders/glass.frag.spv

Ship the .frag beside the .spv so whoever has your mod next can still edit it.


What this folder is not
-----------------------

There is no game here, and no game data. The Forge reads and writes YOUR mod
folder and nothing else; your saves and the base game's files are untouched by
it. If you want to look at how the base game builds something, open its files
in the game folder with a text editor - this tool will not edit them for you.
